cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Chiquipoli: interval and exact verification for the local maximality of A16"
abstract: >-
  Interval-arithmetic and exact-rational certification of the first-order
  hypotheses for the Bingane-Audet equilateral small hexadecagon, with a Lean 4
  formalisation of the criterion itself, so that the passage from the certified
  data to strict local maximality is kernel checked end to end. Also covered:
  the Bingane-Audet family A16 to A1024 in Julia, and A16 to A256 in Lean by
  kernel-checked data. A Lean proof shows, for every n = 16k, that the polygon
  built by the published constructor is feasible and a strict local maximiser
  of the perimeter. An explicit radius of strict local maximality is given for
  A16.
type: software
version: "1.3.1"
date-released: "2026-09-30"
license: MIT
